{
  "analysis": "The input files are available. The plasmid contains the DHFR protein sequence (from the folA CDS translation). The pdb_ids.txt lists 20 PDB entries. The antibody.fasta contains heavy and light chain sequences with a C-terminal His-tag on the heavy chain. I now need to: fetch PDB sequences for all listed IDs, identify which PDB entries correspond to the donor/acceptor fluorescent proteins and the molecule-binding protein, identify the antibody target protein, query fpbase for spectral data, then assemble and validate the gBlock.",
  "plan": "I will run a Python script that uses the available internet APIs to gather all needed data in parallel: (1) fetch FASTA sequences for all PDB IDs from the RCSB API, (2) query fpbase API for fluorescent protein spectra, (3) query PubChem to identify the SMILES molecule, (4) search RCSB for structures containing the SMILES ligand, and (5) attempt to identify the antibody target by searching the PDB for matching antibody sequences. This will give me the information needed to select the correct protein components.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'
import urllib.request, urllib.parse, json, time

# 1. Fetch PDB FASTA for all IDs
ids = open('/app/pdb_ids.txt').read().split()
print("=== PDB FASTA FETCH ===")
for pid in ids:
    url = f"https://www.rcsb.org/fasta/entry/{pid}/display"
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=15) as r:
            data = r.read().decode()
        lines = data.strip().split('\n')
        headers = [l for l in lines if l.startswith('>')]
        seqs = []
        cur = []
        for l in lines:
            if l.startswith('>'):
                if cur:
                    seqs.append(''.join(cur)); cur=[]
            else:
                cur.append(l.strip())
        if cur: seqs.append(''.join(cur))
        print(f"\n{pid}: {len(seqs)} chain(s)")
        for h,s in zip(headers, seqs):
            print(f"  {h[:100]}")
            print(f"  seq_len={len(s)} seq_start={s[:60]}")
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"{pid}: ERROR {e}")
    time.sleep(0.2)

# 2. Try fpbase API endpoints
print("\n=== FPBASE API ===")
for endpoint in ["https://www.fpbase.org/api/proteins/", "https://www.fpbase.org/api/spectra/", "https://fpbase.org/api/proteins/"]:
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(endpoint, timeout=15) as r:
            data = r.read().decode()
        print(f"{endpoint}: {len(data)} bytes, start={data[:200]}")
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"{endpoint}: ERROR {e}")

# 3. PubChem for SMILES molecule
print("\n=== PUBCHEM ===")
smiles = "Nc3nc(OCc1ccccc1)c2nc[nH]c2n3"
encoded = urllib.parse.quote(smiles)
url = f"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/smiles/{encoded}/property/Title,IUPACName,CanonicalSMILES/JSON"
try:
    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=15) as r:
        data = json.loads(r.read())
    print(json.dumps(data, indent=2)[:500])
except Exception as e:
    print(f"PubChem: ERROR {e}")

# 4. Search RCSB by SMILES
print("\n=== RCSB LIGAND SEARCH ===")
query = {
    "query": {
        "type": "terminal",
        "service": "chemical",
        "parameters": {
            "value": smiles,
            "type": "exact"
        }
    },
    "return_type": "entry",
    "request_options": {"return_all_hits": True}
}
try:
    req = urllib.request.Request("https://search.rcsb.org/rcsbsearch/v2/query",
                                 data=json.dumps(query).encode(),
                                 headers={"Content-Type":"application/json"})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:
        data = json.loads(r.read())
    print(json.dumps(data, indent=2)[:1000])
except Exception as e:
    print(f"RCSB search: ERROR {e}")

